rface]\n  - rxn_015: mol_014, mol_005, mol_002 -> mol_016 (Direct Strecker on butanal (alternative route)) [Surface]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Strecker Pathway via Isobutyraldehyde (3 steps)\n  - P2: Reductive Amination via Alpha-Ketoisovalerate (5 steps)\n  - P3: Nitrile Hydrolysis via Isobutyronitrile (4 steps)\n  - P4: Direct amination of isovaleric acid route (2 steps)\n  - P5: Aldol Branching from Acetone and Pyruvate (5 steps)\n  - P6: Chain Elongation via Butanal (4 steps)\n  - P7: Strecker on Butanal plus Branching (5 steps)\n  - P8: Lactic Acid to Acetone and Aldol Branching (6 steps)\n  - P9: Direct Pyruvate Surface Branching Pathway (4 steps)\n  - P10: Retro-synthetic Combination via Propanal (5 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\nSummary: 15 reactions | 3 balanced as written | 0 balanceable with coefficients | 12 UNBALANCED | 0 unchecked\n  - rxn_001 UNBALANCED: CO2 + CH4 + H2 -> CH3COCOOH | reactants minus products: C-1, H+2, O-1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product; H2 as product; CO as reactant; O2 as product\n  - rxn_002 UNBALANCED: CH2O + CH3COCOOH -> CH3CH(OH)COOH | reactants minus products: C+1, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2 as reactant; CO as product\n  - rxn_004 UNBALANCED: CH3COCOOH + CH3COCHO -> CH3CH(CH3)COCOOH | reactants minus products: C+1, H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product; H2 as product; CO as reactant; O2 as product\n  - rxn_005 UNBALANCED: CH3CH(OH)COOH -> CH3COCHO | reactants minus products: O+2 | balanceable if adding: O2 as product\n  - rxn_006 UNBALANCED: CH3CH(CH3)COCOOH + NH3 + H2 -> C5H11NO2 | reactants minus products: H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product\n  - rxn_007 UNBALANCED: CH3CH(CH3)CHO + HCN + NH3 -> C5H11NO2 | reactants minu