ous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"mildly alkaline, wet-dry cycling\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Enolization of formaldehyde, followed by addition to a second formaldehyde and reduction yields acetaldehyde.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Montmorillonite is known to promote C-C bond formation from formaldehyde (Cleaves et al., 2012; Ertem, 2014).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_003\",\n      \"name\": \"Acetaldehyde reduction to ethanol and oxidation to acetone\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_006\", \"mol_002\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_012\", \"mol_004\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"Fe3O4\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"330-350K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"magnetite (Fe3O4)\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": null\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Disproportionation: One acetaldehyde is reduced to ethanol, the other oxidized to acetone with H2 as reductant.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Supported by Fe3O4 redox catalysis experiments (Huber & W\u00e4chtersh\u00e4user, 1997).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_004\",\n      \"name\": \"Aldol condensation of acetone and formaldehyde to 3-methylbutanal\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_012\", \"mol_005\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_011\", \"mol_004\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"montmorillonite\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"320-340K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"1 atm\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"montmorillonite\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"wet-dry cycling\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Enolate of acetone adds to formaldehyde, followed by dehydration, forming 3-methylbutanal.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Aldol reactions on clays are robust under these conditions (Ertem & Ferris, 1996).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_005\",\n      \"name\": \"Strecker synthesis of 2-amino-3-methylbutanenitrile\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_0